### Configuration and Services

#### `FlowConfig.java`

```java
import org.springframework.ai.embedding.EmbeddingModel;
import org.springframework.ai.openai.OpenAiEmbeddingModel;
import org.springframework.ai.openai.api.OpenAiApi;
import org.springframework.ai.vectorstore.VectorStore;
import org.springframework.ai.vectorstore.mongodb.MongoDBAtlasVectorStore;
import org.springframework.ai.vectorstore.mongodb.MongoDBAtlasVectorStoreConfig;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

@Configuration
public class FlowConfig {

    @Value("${spring.data.mongodb.uri}")
    private String mongoUri;

    @Value("${spring.data.mongodb.database}")
    private String mongoDatabase;

    @Value("${spring.ai.openai.api-key}")
    private String openAiApiKey;

    @Bean
    public EmbeddingModel embeddingModel() {
        OpenAiApi openAiApi = new OpenAiApi(openAiApiKey);
        return new OpenAiEmbeddingModel(openAiApi, "text-embedding-3-small", 1536);
    }

    @Bean
    public VectorStore vectorStore(EmbeddingModel embeddingModel) {
        MongoDBAtlasVectorStoreConfig config = MongoDBAtlasVectorStoreConfig.builder()
                .withMongoURI(mongoUri)
                .withDatabaseName(mongoDatabase)
                .withCollectionName("java_vector_team_a")
                .withVectorIndexName("vector_index")
                .build();
        return new MongoDBAtlasVectorStore(config, embeddingModel);
    }

    @Bean
    public VectorCreationService vectorCreationService(VectorStore vectorStore) {
        return new VectorCreationService(vectorStore);
    }

    @Bean
    public VectorSearchService vectorSearchService(VectorStore vectorStore) {
        return new VectorSearchService(vectorStore);
    }
}
```

- **Notes**:
  - `MongoDBAtlasVectorStore` handles all MongoDB interactions internally.
  - Configures `java_vector_team_a` as the collection and `vector_index` as the index name.

#### `VectorCreationService.java`

Uses Spring AI to create and store embeddings:

```java
import org.springframework.ai.document.Document;
import org.springframework.ai.vectorstore.VectorStore;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;

public class VectorCreationService {

    private final VectorStore vectorStore;

    public VectorCreationService(VectorStore vectorStore) {
        this.vectorStore = vectorStore;
    }

    public void createAndStoreEmbeddings() {
        List<String> sampleTexts = Arrays.asList(
            "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.",
            "A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.",
            "To be or not to be, that is the question.",
            "All that glitters is not gold.",
            "The early bird catches the worm."
        );

        // Clear existing data (Spring AI doesn’t provide a direct drop, so we rely on manual cleanup if needed)
        List<Document> documents = sampleTexts.stream()
                .map(text -> {
                    Map<String, Object> metadata = new HashMap<>();
                    metadata.put("source", "sample_text");
                    return new Document(text, metadata);
                })
                .toList();

        vectorStore.add(documents);
        System.out.println("Embeddings created and stored in java_vector_team_a");

        // Create vector index manually via MongoDB Shell or Atlas UI (see below)
    }
}
```

- **Notes**:
  - `vectorStore.add()` generates embeddings with `text-embedding-3-small` and stores them.
  - Spring AI doesn’t directly manage index creation in `1.0.0-M6`, so we’ll create it manually once.

#### `VectorSearchService.java`

Uses Spring AI for retrieval:

```java
import org.springframework.ai.document.Document;
import org.springframework.ai.vectorstore.VectorStore;
import java.util.List;

public class VectorSearchService {

    private final VectorStore vectorStore;

    public VectorSearchService(VectorStore vectorStore) {
        this.vectorStore = vectorStore;
    }

    public List<Document> retrieve(String query) {
        try {
            List<Document> results = vectorStore.similaritySearch(query, 5); // Top 5 results
            System.out.println("Search Successful: " + results.size());
            return results.stream()
                    .filter(doc -> {
                        // Similarity score isn’t directly exposed; assume metadata or filter manually in Atlas
                        return true; // Adjust if score threshold needed
                    })
                    .toList();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("Search Failed: " + e.getMessage());
            e.printStackTrace();
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
```

- **Notes**:
  - `similaritySearch(query, k)` performs the vector search.
  - Spring AI `1.0.0-M6` doesn’t expose the similarity score directly in `Document`, so we’ll rely on Atlas’s ordering (highest dot product first).

#### `VectorController.java`

```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestParam;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;
import org.springframework.ai.document.Document;
import java.util.List;

@RestController
public class VectorController {

    @Autowired
    private VectorCreationService vectorCreationService;

    @Autowired
    private VectorSearchService vectorSearchService;

    @GetMapping("/create-embeddings")
    public String createEmbeddings() {
        vectorCreationService.createAndStoreEmbeddings();
        return "Embeddings created and stored in java_vector_team_a";
    }

    @GetMapping("/search")
    public List<Document> search(@RequestParam String query) {
        return vectorSearchService.retrieve(query);
    }
}
```

